I sit down on a chair in the waiting room.
The room is almost completely quiet.
I sit down and wait patiently.
I feel really bad today.
A mother and a little boy sit opposite me.
The boy is maybe five years old.
He holds a hand on his right ear.
"Ouch, my ear hurts!" he says loudly.
His mother looks at him.
"I know, sweetie," she says gently.
"But it hurts a lot!" the boy complains.
"The doctor ought to call us soon," the mother says.
She puts an arm around his shoulders.
The boy sighs loudly.
He looks very tired.
I understand him well.
My own throat really hurts too.
I just want to feel well again.
